;; SEALS, STAMPS AND SIGNATURES: candidates, their words, and the `seal` nodes (P7.7; SPEC 9.5 defence 5, 10.7; D016, D205, D400-D405). emon's own
;; module (D039). The VERDICTS on the words are rows of `emon.fuserules` (block 400, tried before every other block: `fr-order`); this module measures
;; what those rows read (which groups lie in a seal) and writes the placeholders:
;;
;;   (sm-find pa pts gl fw et epages cg refs owords np sm scr)
;;       Before arbitration, over the document's evidence: the seal, stamp and signature CANDIDATES of every page, one row each of the layer's `sl` arena
;;       (SPEC 9.7: page, box, kind, ink row (-1), primitive reference (`paths`, the path), confidence, the OCR words inside as a `refs` run, flags, and in
;;       the three spare cells the node's text (an `etext` run) and its colour), and the flag `plg-in-seal` on every correspondence group whose words are the
;;       candidate's: arbitration reads that flag as the group column `ag-seal`, and rows 401 and 402 keep the group out of the body.
;;   (sm-write sm et on oa orr text nodes attrs regions nm)
;;       After the Model is built and restructured: a COPY of the body into the empty arenas `nodes attrs regions` (as `emon.restruct` makes one, whose `rs-node`
;;       and `rs-remap` it uses), with a `seal` node (subkind seal, stamp or signature; `color` by `sm-hue`; the words as `text`, flagged `low-conf`) inserted
;;       in READING ORDER: after the last top-level block that covers most of it (a stamp is drawn over the text it belongs to: at least a twentieth of its
;;       box, and at least half as much as any other block), else before the first block that starts below its top. `pa-build` is not touched.
;;
;; WHAT A CANDIDATE IS HERE (D400). The tracer's primitives (P6.4's `ring`, `circle`, `ellipse`, a coloured `rect`) and its colour-layer components need pixels,
;; and a replayed transcript holds none (a replay "reads no pixel", D259): a gate could not run what it asks. The same shapes are in a born-digital page's VECTOR
;; paths (`pa`, with their geometry in `pts`) and the same inks in its glyphs' colours, so the candidates are read from those, which every host answers identically:
;;
;;   a SEAL       a stroked, unfilled path that is ROUND (its end points all within `sm-round` of one radius from their common centre; at least four
;;                Bezier segments), of radius at least `sm-seal-min` (8 mm), that holds words of its own ink or turned along its arc (below), or has another round
;;                path inside it (the double ring);
;;   a STAMP      a stroked, unfilled quadrilateral (rotated or not) with a border at least `sm-stamp-width` (1.5 pt), of a chromatic ink, that holds words of
;;                that ink;
;;   a SIGNATURE  stroked, unfilled, open curves no wider than `sm-sig-width`, merged where they lie within `sm-sig-gap`, at least `sm-sig-segs` Bezier segments,
;;                wider than high, within `sm-cue-lines` line heights of a CUE: a text-layer word `signature`, `signed`, `sign` followed by `here`, or `by:`,
;;                case-folded. Its words are none (the typed name beside it is body text).
;;
;; A WORD OF A SEAL OR STAMP is a text-layer word whose centre is inside the candidate and (its first glyph's fill is within `sm-ink-dist` of the candidate's ink
;; and chromatic) or (the candidate is round and the word is TURNED: its rotation at least `sm-arc-turn` off every right angle, in the ring between half the
;; radius and the ring itself: the arc text of a seal, where the glyphs' rotation varies along the ring). Ordinary body text under a stamp is neither (its
;; ink is the body's and it stands upright), so it stays body: the contract of rule 110 is not touched (D401).
;; An OCR-ONLY group (no text-layer word) whose words' centres all lie inside a seal, a stamp or a signature is the ring's or the stroke's own ink read as
;; letters: it joins the candidate (its words are the node's text only when the candidate has no text-layer word).
;;
;; WHAT IS NOT HERE (D402): the tracer's colour-layer components and primitives (no pixels in a replay; the page unit does not wire P6.3/P6.4 and nothing in a
;; fused born-digital page asks for them), so a seal that is only RASTER (an image placement) or only outlined is no candidate; raster pages (scans, the
;; `scan-ovl` variants and mapo80) are not fused until P7.S. The candidate row keeps its ink-row and primitive cells for them.
(ns emon.sealmark
  (:require [emon.lang :refer [I32 I64 Cells i64 mul64 add64]]
            [emon.port :refer [cells-len cells-at cells-set cells-push cells-drop]]
            [emon.evidence :refer [pa-get pa-count pt-get gl-get ow-get hd-x0 hd-y0 hd-x1 hd-y1 hd-page hd-tstart hd-tlen rf-add
                                   pf-page pf-kind pf-x0 pf-y0 pf-x1 pf-y1 pf-fill pf-stroke pf-width pf-flags pf-pfirst pf-pcount
                                   ptf-x ptf-y ptf-op gf-fill ea-paths ea-owords ev-page-row ep-get epf-width epf-height
                                   pg-closed pg-filled pg-stroked pg-clip pa-curve pa-rect pa-other po-move po-line po-curve po-close]]
            [emon.player :refer [cg-count cg-get cg-set cgf-page cgf-tfirst cgf-tcount cgf-ofirst cgf-ocount cgf-hcount cgf-flags plg-in-seal
                                 sl-new sl-count sl-get pls-seal pls-stamp pls-signature]]
            [emon.model :refer [node-count node-kind node-parent node-region-head node-region-count node-next region-next
                                region-page region-x0 region-y0 region-x1 region-y1
                                node-new node-set-text node-set-sub node-set-conf node-add-flag node-add-src node-add-region node-add-attr-text
                                text-append-cp nk-document nk-section nk-heading nk-paragraph nk-list nk-table nk-figure nk-quote nk-code nk-note
                                nk-formula nk-caption nk-seal nk-furniture fk-color fl-low-conf sr-text sr-ocr sr-infer]]
            [emon.restruct :refer [rs-node rs-remap]]
            [kin.lang :refer [defn defdata return let set while if do comment
                              + - * < > <= >= == != and or quot rem bit-and bit-or]]))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- the settings (SPEC 13: named, first values; P10.1 calibrates)

(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-seal-min [] (comment "`seal-min`: the radius (centipoints) a ring needs to be a seal: 8 mm.") (return 2268))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-stamp-width [] (comment "`stamp-width`: the border (centipoints) a stamp's rectangle needs: 1.5 pt.") (return 150))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-sig-width [] (comment "`sig-width`: the widest stroke (centipoints) of a pen signature.") (return 250))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-sig-gap [] (comment "`sig-gap`: how far (centipoints) strokes of one signature lie apart.") (return 800))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-sig-segs [] (comment "`sig-segs`: the Bezier segments a signature has, together.") (return 3))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-sig-min-w [] (comment "The width (centipoints) a signature needs: 30 pt.") (return 3000))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-cue-lines [] (comment "`cue-lines`: how many line heights from a cue a signature may lie.") (return 3))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-round [] (comment "`seal-round`: how far (per cent of the radius) a ring's end points may lie from the circle.") (return 8))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-square [] (comment "How far (per cent) a ring's box may be from a square.") (return 12))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-chroma [] (comment "`ink-chroma`: the spread (0-255) between the largest and smallest channel of a chromatic ink.") (return 48))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-ink-dist [] (comment "`sm-ink-dist`: how far apart (sum of the channel differences) two inks may be and be one.") (return 192))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-arc-turn [] (comment "`arc-turn`: how far (centi-degrees) off every right angle a word of a seal's arc is turned.") (return 100))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-page-share [] (comment "The share of the page (per mille) a stamp's box may cover: a coloured frame round the page is no stamp.") (return 350))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-overlap [] (comment "`seal-overlap`: the share (per cent) of a candidate's box a top-level block must cover for the candidate to be written after it.") (return 5))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-max-cands [] (comment "The most candidates of one page (a hostile page's strokes).") (return 64))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-max-strokes [] (comment "The most signature strokes of one page that are clustered.") (return 96))

;; the candidate record in the page scratch: 12 cells
;; 0 kind (`pls`; 0 dropped), 1 path row, 2-5 box, 6 centre x, 7 centre y, 8 radius (0 for a stamp or a signature), 9 ink (0xRRGGBB, -1),
;; 10 flags (1 chromatic, 2 double ring, 4 inside another ring, 8 turned words, 16 ink words), 11 members (text-layer words)
(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-cw [] (return 12))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- colours

(defn ^I32 sm-abs [^I32 v]
  (if (< v 0) (return (- 0 v)))
  (return v))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-spread [^I32 rgb]
  (comment "The spread between the largest and the smallest channel of 0xRRGGBB; 0 for a colour that is unknown (negative).")
  (if (< rgb 0) (return 0))
  (let [^I32 r (rem (quot rgb 65536) 256)
        ^I32 g (rem (quot rgb 256) 256)
        ^I32 b (rem rgb 256)
        ^:mut ^I32 mx r
        ^:mut ^I32 mn r]
    (if (> g mx) (set mx g))
    (if (> b mx) (set mx b))
    (if (< g mn) (set mn g))
    (if (< b mn) (set mn b))
    (return (- mx mn))))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-ink-near [^I32 a ^I32 b]
  (comment "1 when both inks are known and the sum of their channel differences is at most `sm-ink-dist`.")
  (if (< a 0) (return 0))
  (if (< b 0) (return 0))
  (let [^I32 d (+ (sm-abs (- (rem (quot a 65536) 256) (rem (quot b 65536) 256)))
                  (+ (sm-abs (- (rem (quot a 256) 256) (rem (quot b 256) 256)))
                     (sm-abs (- (rem a 256) (rem b 256)))))]
    (if (<= d (sm-ink-dist)) (return 1))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-hue [^I32 rgb]
  (comment "The colour name of an ink, a code of `sm-names` (the 12 hue buckets of 30 degrees that gold colours use, and black, gray and white for an ink with")
  (comment "no chroma): 0 black 1 gray 2 white 3 red 4 orange 5 yellow 6 lime 7 green 8 teal 9 cyan 10 blue 11 purple 12 magenta 13 pink; -1 unknown.")
  (if (< rgb 0) (return -1))
  (let [^I32 r (rem (quot rgb 65536) 256)
        ^I32 g (rem (quot rgb 256) 256)
        ^I32 b (rem rgb 256)
        ^I32 d (sm-spread rgb)
        ^:mut ^I32 mx r
        ^:mut ^I32 h 0]
    (if (> g mx) (set mx g))
    (if (> b mx) (set mx b))
    (if (< d 32)
      (do (if (< mx 80) (return 0))
          (if (>= mx 200) (return 2))
          (return 1)))
    (if (== mx r)
      (set h (quot (* 60 (- g b)) d))
      (if (== mx g)
        (set h (+ 120 (quot (* 60 (- b r)) d)))
        (set h (+ 240 (quot (* 60 (- r g)) d)))))
    (if (< h 0) (set h (+ h 360)))
    (if (< h 15) (return 3))
    (if (< h 45) (return 4))
    (if (< h 70) (return 5))
    (if (< h 95) (return 6))
    (if (< h 165) (return 7))
    (if (< h 190) (return 8))
    (if (< h 215) (return 9))
    (if (< h 255) (return 10))
    (if (< h 290) (return 11))
    (if (< h 325) (return 12))
    (if (< h 345) (return 13))
    (return 3)))

(defdata ^:pub sm-names
  :emitter kin.lang/flat-array
  :data [98 108 97 99 107
         103 114 97 121
         119 104 105 116 101
         114 101 100
         111 114 97 110 103 101
         121 101 108 108 111 119
         108 105 109 101
         103 114 101 101 110
         116 101 97 108
         99 121 97 110
         98 108 117 101
         112 117 114 112 108 101
         109 97 103 101 110 116 97
         112 105 110 107]
  :accessors {^I32 sm-name-at [^I32 ignored ^I32 i]})

(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-name-off [^I32 c]
  (if (== c 0) (return 0))
  (if (== c 1) (return 5))
  (if (== c 2) (return 9))
  (if (== c 3) (return 14))
  (if (== c 4) (return 17))
  (if (== c 5) (return 23))
  (if (== c 6) (return 29))
  (if (== c 7) (return 33))
  (if (== c 8) (return 38))
  (if (== c 9) (return 42))
  (if (== c 10) (return 46))
  (if (== c 11) (return 50))
  (if (== c 12) (return 56))
  (return 63))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-name-len [^I32 c]
  (if (== c 0) (return 5))
  (if (== c 1) (return 4))
  (if (== c 2) (return 5))
  (if (== c 3) (return 3))
  (if (== c 4) (return 6))
  (if (== c 5) (return 6))
  (if (== c 6) (return 4))
  (if (== c 7) (return 5))
  (if (== c 8) (return 4))
  (if (== c 9) (return 4))
  (if (== c 10) (return 4))
  (if (== c 11) (return 6))
  (if (== c 12) (return 7))
  (return 4))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- rings

(defn ^I32 sm-in-disc [^I32 dx ^I32 dy ^I32 r ^I32 pct]
  (comment "1 when the point (dx, dy) from a centre is inside the disc of radius r * pct / 100.")
  (let [^I64 d2 (add64 (mul64 (i64 dx) (i64 dx)) (mul64 (i64 dy) (i64 dy)))
        ^I64 lhs (mul64 d2 (i64 10000))
        ^I64 rhs (mul64 (mul64 (i64 r) (i64 r)) (i64 (* pct pct)))]
    (if (<= lhs rhs) (return 1))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-ring-test [^Cells pa ^Cells pts ^I32 r ^:mut ^Cells out]
  (comment "1 when path row r is a round closed path of at least four Bezier segments: its end points (the first point of a subpath and the last of each")
  (comment "Bezier triple) all within `sm-round` per cent of one radius from the centre of their box, the box a square within `sm-square` per cent. The")
  (comment "centre and radius are written to out[0..2], out[3] says whether the roundness was not verified. A path whose geometry was not kept (pcount 0) is no ring.")
  (let [^I32 n (pa-get pa r (pf-pcount))
        ^I32 f (pa-get pa r (pf-pfirst))
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 x0 2000000000
        ^:mut ^I32 y0 2000000000
        ^:mut ^I32 x1 -2000000000
        ^:mut ^I32 y1 -2000000000
        ^:mut ^I32 ne 0
        ^:mut ^I32 segs 0
        ^:mut ^I32 e 0
        ^:mut ^I32 op 0
        ^:mut ^I32 x 0
        ^:mut ^I32 y 0]
    (comment "a path of more than `PATH_KEEP` points keeps its box only (Chrome draws a circle in some forty Bezier segments): a curve whose box, less its")
    (comment "stroke, is a square is taken for a ring, the roundness unverified (out[3] is 1)")
    (if (or (< f 0) (== n 0))
      (do (if (!= (pa-get pa r (pf-kind)) (pa-curve)) (return 0))
          (set x0 (+ (pa-get pa r (pf-x0)) (quot (pa-get pa r (pf-width)) 2)))
          (set y0 (+ (pa-get pa r (pf-y0)) (quot (pa-get pa r (pf-width)) 2)))
          (set x1 (- (pa-get pa r (pf-x1)) (quot (pa-get pa r (pf-width)) 2)))
          (set y1 (- (pa-get pa r (pf-y1)) (quot (pa-get pa r (pf-width)) 2)))
          (let [^I32 w (- x1 x0)
                ^I32 h (- y1 y0)
                ^:mut ^I32 big w
                ^:mut ^I32 small h]
            (if (< w h) (do (set big h) (set small w)))
            (if (<= big 0) (return 0))
            (if (> (* (- big small) 100) (* big (sm-square))) (return 0))
            (cells-set out 0 (quot (+ x0 x1) 2))
            (cells-set out 1 (quot (+ y0 y1) 2))
            (cells-set out 2 (quot (+ w h) 4))
            (cells-set out 3 1)
            (return 1))))
    (if (< n 10) (return 0))
    (cells-set out 3 0)
    (comment "the end points: their box first")
    (while (< j n)
      (do (set op (pt-get pts (+ f j) (ptf-op)))
          (set e -1)
          (if (or (== op (po-move)) (== op (po-line)))
            (do (set e j)
                (set j (+ j 1)))
            (if (== op (po-curve))
              (do (if (< (+ j 2) n) (set e (+ j 2)))
                  (set segs (+ segs 1))
                  (set j (+ j 3)))
              (set j (+ j 1))))
          (if (>= e 0)
            (do (set x (pt-get pts (+ f e) (ptf-x)))
                (set y (pt-get pts (+ f e) (ptf-y)))
                (if (< x x0) (set x0 x))
                (if (< y y0) (set y0 y))
                (if (> x x1) (set x1 x))
                (if (> y y1) (set y1 y))
                (set ne (+ ne 1))))))
    (if (< segs 4) (return 0))
    (let [^I32 w (- x1 x0)
          ^I32 h (- y1 y0)
          ^:mut ^I32 big w
          ^:mut ^I32 small h
          ^I32 cx (quot (+ x0 x1) 2)
          ^I32 cy (quot (+ y0 y1) 2)
          ^I32 rad (quot (+ w h) 4)]
      (if (< w h) (do (set big h) (set small w)))
      (if (<= big 0) (return 0))
      (if (> (* (- big small) 100) (* big (sm-square))) (return 0))
      (set j 0)
      (while (< j n)
        (do (set op (pt-get pts (+ f j) (ptf-op)))
            (set e -1)
            (if (or (== op (po-move)) (== op (po-line)))
              (do (set e j)
                  (set j (+ j 1)))
              (if (== op (po-curve))
                (do (if (< (+ j 2) n) (set e (+ j 2)))
                    (set j (+ j 3)))
                (set j (+ j 1))))
            (if (>= e 0)
              (do (set x (- (pt-get pts (+ f e) (ptf-x)) cx))
                  (set y (- (pt-get pts (+ f e) (ptf-y)) cy))
                  (if (== (sm-in-disc x y rad (+ 100 (sm-round))) 0) (return 0))
                  (if (== (sm-in-disc x y rad (- 100 (sm-round))) 1) (return 0))))))
      (cells-set out 0 cx)
      (cells-set out 1 cy)
      (cells-set out 2 rad)
      (cells-set out 3 0)
      (return 1))))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- words

(defn ^I32 sm-fold [^I32 c]
  (if (and (>= c 65) (<= c 90)) (return (+ c 32)))
  (return c))

(defn ^I32 sm-word-is [^Cells fw ^Cells et ^I32 row ^I32 pre0 ^I32 pre1 ^I32 pre2 ^I32 pre3 ^I32 pre4 ^I32 pre5 ^I32 pre6 ^I32 pre7 ^I32 pre8 ^I32 want]
  (comment "1 when word `row` starts, case-folded, with the code points pre0..pre(want-1) (nine at most).")
  (let [^I32 ts (cells-at fw (+ (* row 24) 11))
        ^I32 tl (cells-at fw (+ (* row 24) 12))]
    (if (< tl want) (return 0))
    (if (!= (sm-fold (cells-at et ts)) pre0) (return 0))
    (if (and (> want 1) (!= (sm-fold (cells-at et (+ ts 1))) pre1)) (return 0))
    (if (and (> want 2) (!= (sm-fold (cells-at et (+ ts 2))) pre2)) (return 0))
    (if (and (> want 3) (!= (sm-fold (cells-at et (+ ts 3))) pre3)) (return 0))
    (if (and (> want 4) (!= (sm-fold (cells-at et (+ ts 4))) pre4)) (return 0))
    (if (and (> want 5) (!= (sm-fold (cells-at et (+ ts 5))) pre5)) (return 0))
    (if (and (> want 6) (!= (sm-fold (cells-at et (+ ts 6))) pre6)) (return 0))
    (if (and (> want 7) (!= (sm-fold (cells-at et (+ ts 7))) pre7)) (return 0))
    (if (and (> want 8) (!= (sm-fold (cells-at et (+ ts 8))) pre8)) (return 0))
    (return 1)))

(defn ^I32 sm-cue-word [^Cells fw ^Cells et ^I32 row ^I32 end]
  (comment "1 when word `row` (of a page whose words end at `end`) is a signature cue: `signature`, `signed`, `sign` followed by `here`, `by:`; case-folded.")
  (let [^I32 tl (cells-at fw (+ (* row 24) 12))]
    (if (== (sm-word-is fw et row 115 105 103 110 97 116 117 114 101 9) 1) (return 1))
    (if (== (sm-word-is fw et row 115 105 103 110 101 100 0 0 0 6) 1) (return 1))
    (if (and (== tl 3) (== (sm-word-is fw et row 98 121 58 0 0 0 0 0 0 3) 1)) (return 1))
    (if (and (== tl 4) (and (== (sm-word-is fw et row 115 105 103 110 0 0 0 0 0 4) 1) (< (+ row 1) end)))
      (if (== (sm-word-is fw et (+ row 1) 104 101 114 101 0 0 0 0 0 4) 1) (return 1)))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-turned [^I32 rot]
  (comment "1 when the rotation (centi-degrees) is at least `sm-arc-turn` off every right angle.")
  (let [^I32 a (rem (+ (rem rot 9000) 9000) 9000)
        ^:mut ^I32 off a]
    (if (> a 4500) (set off (- 9000 a)))
    (if (>= off (sm-arc-turn)) (return 1))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 sm-word-ink [^Cells fw ^Cells gl ^I32 row]
  (comment "The fill of the first glyph of word `row` (0xRRGGBB), -1 when the word has no glyph or its colour is unknown.")
  (let [^I32 g0 (cells-at fw (+ (* row 24) 17))
        ^I32 gn (cells-at fw (+ (* row 24) 18))]
    (if (<= gn 0) (return -1))
    (return (gl-get gl g0 (gf-fill)))))

;; one candidate (record at `c` of the scratch `scr`) against one box or point: inside?
(defn ^I32 sm-inside [^Cells scr ^I32 c ^I32 cx ^I32 cy]
  (comment "1 when the point lies inside the candidate: in its disc (a ring, 6 per cent beyond) or its box (a stamp or a signature).")
  (if (> (cells-at scr (+ c 8)) 0)
    (return (sm-in-disc (- cx (cells-at scr (+ c 6))) (- cy (cells-at scr (+ c 7))) (cells-at scr (+ c 8)) 106)))
  (if (and (>= cx (cells-at scr (+ c 2))) (and (<= cx (cells-at scr (+ c 4)))
           (and (>= cy (cells-at scr (+ c 3))) (<= cy (cells-at scr (+ c 5))))))
    (return 1))
  (return 0))

(defn ^I32 sm-member [^Cells scr ^I32 c ^Cells fw ^Cells gl ^I32 row]
  (comment "1 when text-layer word `row` belongs to the seal or stamp at record `c` (see the head of this file); 0 for a signature (it has no words).")
  (let [^I32 at (* row 24)
        ^I32 cx (quot (+ (cells-at fw (+ at 1)) (cells-at fw (+ at 3))) 2)
        ^I32 cy (quot (+ (cells-at fw (+ at 2)) (cells-at fw (+ at 4))) 2)
        ^I32 kind (cells-at scr c)
        ^I32 ink (sm-word-ink fw gl row)]
    (if (or (== kind 0) (== kind (pls-signature))) (return 0))
    (if (== (sm-inside scr c cx cy) 0) (return 0))
    (if (and (> (sm-spread ink) (sm-chroma)) (== (sm-ink-near ink (cells-at scr (+ c 9))) 1)) (return 1))
    (if (and (== kind (pls-seal)) (== (sm-turned (cells-at fw (+ at 9))) 1))
      (do (if (== (sm-in-disc (- cx (cells-at scr (+ c 6))) (- cy (cells-at scr (+ c 7))) (cells-at scr (+ c 8)) 50) 0)
            (return 1))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 sm-word-cand [^Cells scr ^I32 ncand ^Cells fw ^Cells gl ^I32 row]
  (comment "The record (cell offset) of the first candidate that text-layer word `row` belongs to, -1 for none.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 k 0]
    (while (< k ncand)
      (do (if (== (sm-member scr (* k (sm-cw)) fw gl row) 1) (return (* k (sm-cw))))
          (set k (+ k 1))))
    (return -1)))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- one page

(defn ^I32 sm-pts-quad [^Cells pa ^Cells pts ^I32 r]
  (comment "1 when path row r is a closed quadrilateral: four corners, joined by lines (the fifth point repeats the first or is its `close`).")
  (let [^I32 n (pa-get pa r (pf-pcount))
        ^I32 f (pa-get pa r (pf-pfirst))
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 op 0
        ^:mut ^I32 corners 0]
    (if (< f 0) (return 0))
    (if (or (< n 4) (> n 6)) (return 0))
    (while (< j n)
      (do (set op (pt-get pts (+ f j) (ptf-op)))
          (if (== op (po-curve)) (return 0))
          (if (or (== op (po-move)) (== op (po-line))) (set corners (+ corners 1)))
          (set j (+ j 1))))
    (if (or (== corners 4) (== corners 5)) (return 1))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 sm-stroke-only [^Cells pa ^I32 r]
  (comment "1 when path row r is stroked and neither filled nor a clip.")
  (let [^I32 fl (pa-get pa r (pf-flags))]
    (if (== (bit-and fl (pg-stroked)) 0) (return 0))
    (if (!= (bit-and fl (pg-filled)) 0) (return 0))
    (if (!= (bit-and fl (pg-clip)) 0) (return 0))
    (return 1)))

(defn ^I32 sm-add-cand [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 kind ^I32 row ^I32 x0 ^I32 y0 ^I32 x1 ^I32 y1 ^I32 cx ^I32 cy ^I32 rad ^I32 ink ^I32 flags]
  (cells-push scr kind)
  (cells-push scr row)
  (cells-push scr x0)
  (cells-push scr y0)
  (cells-push scr x1)
  (cells-push scr y1)
  (cells-push scr cx)
  (cells-push scr cy)
  (cells-push scr rad)
  (cells-push scr ink)
  (cells-push scr flags)
  (cells-push scr 0)
  (return 0))

(defn ^I32 sm-rings [^Cells pa ^Cells pts ^I32 p0 ^I32 p1 ^:mut ^Cells scr ^:mut ^Cells tmp]
  (comment "The ring candidates of the paths [p0, p1) (records in `scr`), and which of them is another's inner ring. `tmp` is eight cells of scratch (the ring test's answer is its first four).")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 r p0
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 m 0
        ^:mut ^I32 n 0
        ^:mut ^I32 a 0
        ^:mut ^I32 b 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ink 0
        ^:mut ^I32 fl 0]
    (while (< r p1)
      (do (if (and (== (sm-stroke-only pa r) 1) (< n (sm-max-cands)))
            (if (== (sm-ring-test pa pts r tmp) 1)
              (if (>= (cells-at tmp 2) (sm-seal-min))
                (do (set ink (pa-get pa r (pf-stroke)))
                    (set fl 0)
                    (if (> (sm-spread ink) (sm-chroma)) (set fl 1))
                    (if (== (cells-at tmp 3) 1) (set fl (+ fl 16)))
                    (sm-add-cand scr (pls-seal) r (- (cells-at tmp 0) (cells-at tmp 2)) (- (cells-at tmp 1) (cells-at tmp 2))
                                 (+ (cells-at tmp 0) (cells-at tmp 2)) (+ (cells-at tmp 1) (cells-at tmp 2))
                                 (cells-at tmp 0) (cells-at tmp 1) (cells-at tmp 2) ink fl)
                    (set n (+ n 1))))))
          (set r (+ r 1))))
    (comment "a ring with another round path inside it (concentric within 8 per cent, between 0.4 and 0.95 of its radius) is a double ring; the inner one is no candidate")
    (set k 0)
    (while (< k n)
      (do (set m 0)
          (while (< m n)
            (do (set a (* k (sm-cw)))
                (set b (* m (sm-cw)))
                (if (and (!= k m) (== (bit-and (cells-at scr (+ b 10)) 4) 0))
                  (if (and (< (* (cells-at scr (+ b 8)) 100) (* (cells-at scr (+ a 8)) 95))
                           (> (* (cells-at scr (+ b 8)) 100) (* (cells-at scr (+ a 8)) 40)))
                    (if (and (<= (* (sm-abs (- (cells-at scr (+ a 6)) (cells-at scr (+ b 6)))) 100) (* (cells-at scr (+ a 8)) 8))
                             (<= (* (sm-abs (- (cells-at scr (+ a 7)) (cells-at scr (+ b 7)))) 100) (* (cells-at scr (+ a 8)) 8)))
                      (do (cells-set scr (+ a 10) (bit-or (cells-at scr (+ a 10)) 2))
                          (cells-set scr (+ b 10) (bit-or (cells-at scr (+ b 10)) 4))))))
                (set m (+ m 1))))
          (set k (+ k 1))))
    (return n)))

(defn ^I32 sm-share-ok [^I32 w ^I32 h ^I32 pw ^I32 ph]
  (comment "1 when a box w x h covers at most `sm-page-share` per mille of a page pw x ph.")
  (let [^I64 lhs (mul64 (mul64 (i64 w) (i64 h)) (i64 1000))
        ^I64 rhs (mul64 (mul64 (i64 pw) (i64 ph)) (i64 (sm-page-share)))]
    (if (<= lhs rhs) (return 1))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 sm-stamps [^Cells pa ^Cells pts ^I32 p0 ^I32 p1 ^I32 pw ^I32 ph ^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 n0]
  (comment "The stamp candidates of the paths [p0, p1): stroked, unfilled quadrilaterals with a border of at least `sm-stamp-width` of a chromatic ink, at least")
  (comment "10 pt on a side and not covering more than `sm-page-share` of the page. Appended to `scr`; answers the candidates in all.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 r p0
        ^:mut ^I32 n n0
        ^:mut ^I32 w 0
        ^:mut ^I32 h 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ink 0]
    (while (< r p1)
      (do (if (and (== (sm-stroke-only pa r) 1) (< n (sm-max-cands)))
            (if (>= (pa-get pa r (pf-width)) (sm-stamp-width))
              (if (== (sm-pts-quad pa pts r) 1)
                (do (set ink (pa-get pa r (pf-stroke)))
                    (set w (- (pa-get pa r (pf-x1)) (pa-get pa r (pf-x0))))
                    (set h (- (pa-get pa r (pf-y1)) (pa-get pa r (pf-y0))))
                    (if (and (> (sm-spread ink) (sm-chroma)) (and (>= w 1000) (>= h 1000)))
                      (if (== (sm-share-ok w h pw ph) 1)
                        (do (sm-add-cand scr (pls-stamp) r (pa-get pa r (pf-x0)) (pa-get pa r (pf-y0)) (pa-get pa r (pf-x1)) (pa-get pa r (pf-y1))
                                         0 0 0 ink 1)
                            (set n (+ n 1)))))))))
          (set r (+ r 1))))
    (return n)))

;; the signature strokes: 6 cells each in `tmp` (from cell 8): box x0 y0 x1 y1, Bezier segments (-1: merged into another), first path row, ink

(defn ^I32 sm-segs [^Cells pa ^Cells pts ^I32 r]
  (comment "The Bezier segments of path row r (a triple of curve points), 0 when its geometry was not kept.")
  (let [^I32 n (pa-get pa r (pf-pcount))
        ^I32 f (pa-get pa r (pf-pfirst))
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 c 0]
    (if (< f 0) (return 0))
    (while (< j n)
      (do (if (== (pt-get pts (+ f j) (ptf-op)) (po-curve)) (set c (+ c 1)))
          (set j (+ j 1))))
    (return (quot c 3))))

(defn ^I32 sm-gap [^I32 a0 ^I32 a1 ^I32 b0 ^I32 b1]
  (comment "The distance between the intervals [a0, a1] and [b0, b1]; 0 when they overlap.")
  (if (> b0 a1) (return (- b0 a1)))
  (if (> a0 b1) (return (- a0 b1)))
  (return 0))

(defn ^I32 sm-signatures [^Cells pa ^Cells pts ^Cells fw ^Cells et ^I32 page ^I32 p0 ^I32 p1 ^I32 pw ^I32 ph ^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 n0 ^:mut ^Cells tmp]
  (comment "The signature candidates of page `page`'s paths [p0, p1): the open, stroked, unfilled curves no wider than `sm-sig-width` (and neither the page's width nor")
  (comment "a third of its height), merged where they lie within `sm-sig-gap`, kept when they have at least `sm-sig-segs` Bezier segments, are at least 30 pt wide and")
  (comment "wider than 1.5 times their height, and a cue word of the page lies within `sm-cue-lines` line heights of the cluster. Appended to `scr`.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 r p0
        ^:mut ^I32 ns 0
        ^:mut ^I32 n n0
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 changed 1
        ^:mut ^I32 a 0
        ^:mut ^I32 b 0
        ^:mut ^I32 w 0
        ^:mut ^I32 h 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cue 0
        ^:mut ^I32 vg 0
        ^:mut ^I32 hg 0
        ^:mut ^I32 lh 0
        ^:mut ^I32 nw (quot (cells-len fw) 24)]
    (cells-drop tmp 8)
    (while (< r p1)
      (do (if (and (== (sm-stroke-only pa r) 1) (< ns (sm-max-strokes)))
            (if (and (== (bit-and (pa-get pa r (pf-flags)) (pg-closed)) 0) (<= (pa-get pa r (pf-width)) (sm-sig-width)))
              (if (== (pa-get pa r (pf-kind)) (pa-curve))
                (if (and (< (- (pa-get pa r (pf-x1)) (pa-get pa r (pf-x0))) pw) (< (* (- (pa-get pa r (pf-y1)) (pa-get pa r (pf-y0))) 3) ph))
                  (do (cells-push tmp (pa-get pa r (pf-x0)))
                      (cells-push tmp (pa-get pa r (pf-y0)))
                      (cells-push tmp (pa-get pa r (pf-x1)))
                      (cells-push tmp (pa-get pa r (pf-y1)))
                      (cells-push tmp (sm-segs pa pts r))
                      (cells-push tmp r)
                      (cells-push tmp (pa-get pa r (pf-stroke)))
                      (set ns (+ ns 1)))))))
          (set r (+ r 1))))
    (comment "merge until nothing merges; a stroke is a record of 7 cells from cell 8 of tmp")
    (while (== changed 1)
      (do (set changed 0)
          (set i 0)
          (while (< i ns)
            (do (set a (+ 8 (* i 7)))
                (if (>= (cells-at tmp (+ a 4)) 0)
                  (do (set j (+ i 1))
                      (while (< j ns)
                        (do (set b (+ 8 (* j 7)))
                            (if (>= (cells-at tmp (+ b 4)) 0)
                              (if (and (<= (sm-gap (cells-at tmp a) (cells-at tmp (+ a 2)) (cells-at tmp b) (cells-at tmp (+ b 2))) (sm-sig-gap))
                                       (<= (sm-gap (cells-at tmp (+ a 1)) (cells-at tmp (+ a 3)) (cells-at tmp (+ b 1)) (cells-at tmp (+ b 3))) (sm-sig-gap)))
                                (do (if (< (cells-at tmp b) (cells-at tmp a)) (cells-set tmp a (cells-at tmp b)))
                                    (if (< (cells-at tmp (+ b 1)) (cells-at tmp (+ a 1))) (cells-set tmp (+ a 1) (cells-at tmp (+ b 1))))
                                    (if (> (cells-at tmp (+ b 2)) (cells-at tmp (+ a 2))) (cells-set tmp (+ a 2) (cells-at tmp (+ b 2))))
                                    (if (> (cells-at tmp (+ b 3)) (cells-at tmp (+ a 3))) (cells-set tmp (+ a 3) (cells-at tmp (+ b 3))))
                                    (cells-set tmp (+ a 4) (+ (cells-at tmp (+ a 4)) (cells-at tmp (+ b 4))))
                                    (cells-set tmp (+ b 4) -1)
                                    (set changed 1))))
                            (set j (+ j 1))))))
                (set i (+ i 1))))))
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i ns)
      (do (set a (+ 8 (* i 7)))
          (set w (- (cells-at tmp (+ a 2)) (cells-at tmp a)))
          (set h (- (cells-at tmp (+ a 3)) (cells-at tmp (+ a 1))))
          (if (and (>= (cells-at tmp (+ a 4)) (sm-sig-segs)) (and (>= w (sm-sig-min-w)) (>= (* w 2) (* h 3))))
            (do (set cue 0)
                (set j 0)
                (while (and (< j nw) (== cue 0))
                  (do (if (== (cells-at fw (* j 24)) page)
                        (if (== (sm-cue-word fw et j nw) 1)
                          (do (set lh (- (cells-at fw (+ (* j 24) 4)) (cells-at fw (+ (* j 24) 2))))
                              (set vg (sm-gap (cells-at tmp (+ a 1)) (cells-at tmp (+ a 3)) (cells-at fw (+ (* j 24) 2)) (cells-at fw (+ (* j 24) 4))))
                              (set hg (sm-gap (cells-at tmp a) (cells-at tmp (+ a 2)) (cells-at fw (+ (* j 24) 1)) (cells-at fw (+ (* j 24) 3))))
                              (if (and (<= vg (* lh (sm-cue-lines))) (<= hg w)) (set cue 1)))))
                      (set j (+ j 1))))
                (if (and (== cue 1) (< n (sm-max-cands)))
                  (do (sm-add-cand scr (pls-signature) (cells-at tmp (+ a 5)) (cells-at tmp a) (cells-at tmp (+ a 1)) (cells-at tmp (+ a 2)) (cells-at tmp (+ a 3))
                                   0 0 0 (cells-at tmp (+ a 6)) 0)
                      (set n (+ n 1))))))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (return n)))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- the words of a candidate

(defn ^I32 sm-group-inside [^Cells cg ^Cells refs ^Cells owords ^I32 g ^Cells scr ^I32 c]
  (comment "1 when the group has no text-layer or hidden word, has OCR words, and the centre of every one lies inside the candidate at record `c`.")
  (let [^I32 no (cg-get cg g (cgf-ocount))
        ^I32 of (cg-get cg g (cgf-ofirst))
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 row 0]
    (if (> (cg-get cg g (cgf-tcount)) 0) (return 0))
    (if (> (cg-get cg g (cgf-hcount)) 0) (return 0))
    (if (== no 0) (return 0))
    (if (== (cells-at scr c) 0) (return 0))
    (while (< k no)
      (do (set row (cells-at refs (+ (* (+ of k) 2) 1)))
          (if (== (sm-inside scr c (quot (+ (ow-get owords row (hd-x0)) (ow-get owords row (hd-x1))) 2)
                             (quot (+ (ow-get owords row (hd-y0)) (ow-get owords row (hd-y1))) 2)) 0)
            (return 0))
          (set k (+ k 1))))
    (return 1)))

(defn ^I32 sm-word-len [^Cells fw ^I32 row]
  (return (cells-at fw (+ (* row 24) 12))))

(defn ^I32 sm-cx [^Cells fw ^I32 row] (return (quot (+ (cells-at fw (+ (* row 24) 1)) (cells-at fw (+ (* row 24) 3))) 2)))
(defn ^I32 sm-cy [^Cells fw ^I32 row] (return (quot (+ (cells-at fw (+ (* row 24) 2)) (cells-at fw (+ (* row 24) 4))) 2)))

(defn ^I32 sm-push-run [^:mut ^Cells et ^I32 ts ^I32 tl]
  (let [^:mut ^I32 j 0]
    (while (< j tl)
      (do (cells-push et (cells-at et (+ ts j)))
          (set j (+ j 1))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 sm-count-members [^Cells scr ^I32 c ^Cells fw ^Cells gl ^I32 page]
  (let [^I32 nfw (quot (cells-len fw) 24)
        ^:mut ^I32 w 0
        ^:mut ^I32 n 0]
    (while (< w nfw)
      (do (if (== (cells-at fw (* w 24)) page)
            (if (== (sm-member scr c fw gl w) 1) (set n (+ n 1))))
          (set w (+ w 1))))
    (return n)))

(defn ^I32 sm-text-layer-text [^Cells scr ^I32 c ^Cells fw ^Cells gl ^:mut ^Cells et ^I32 page]
  (comment "Append to `et` the words of the candidate at record `c`, in the text layer's order, one space between two words unless both are one glyph and no wider")
  (comment "apart than 1.4 times the mean step of the single glyphs (the arc text of a seal: a glyph a word, the spaces of the ring are no word).")
  (let [^I32 nfw (quot (cells-len fw) 24)
        ^:mut ^I32 w 0
        ^:mut ^I32 prev -1
        ^:mut ^I32 sum 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cnt 0
        ^:mut ^I32 d 0
        ^:mut ^I32 mean 0]
    (while (< w nfw)
      (do (if (== (cells-at fw (* w 24)) page)
            (if (== (sm-member scr c fw gl w) 1)
              (do (if (>= prev 0)
                    (if (and (== (sm-word-len fw prev) 1) (== (sm-word-len fw w) 1))
                      (do (set sum (+ sum (+ (sm-abs (- (sm-cx fw w) (sm-cx fw prev))) (sm-abs (- (sm-cy fw w) (sm-cy fw prev))))))
                          (set cnt (+ cnt 1)))))
                  (set prev w))))
          (set w (+ w 1))))
    (if (> cnt 0) (set mean (quot sum cnt)))
    (set w 0)
    (set prev -1)
    (while (< w nfw)
      (do (if (== (cells-at fw (* w 24)) page)
            (if (== (sm-member scr c fw gl w) 1)
              (do (if (>= prev 0)
                    (do (set d (+ (sm-abs (- (sm-cx fw w) (sm-cx fw prev))) (sm-abs (- (sm-cy fw w) (sm-cy fw prev)))))
                        (if (or (or (!= (sm-word-len fw prev) 1) (!= (sm-word-len fw w) 1)) (> (* d 10) (* mean 14)))
                          (cells-push et 32))))
                  (sm-push-run et (cells-at fw (+ (* w 24) 11)) (cells-at fw (+ (* w 24) 12)))
                  (set prev w))))
          (set w (+ w 1))))
    (return 0)))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- one page's candidates, accepted and written

(defn ^I32 sm-page [^Cells scr ^I32 n ^I32 page ^Cells fw ^Cells gl ^:mut ^Cells et ^:mut ^Cells cg ^:mut ^Cells refs ^Cells owords ^:mut ^Cells sm]
  (comment "Keep the candidates of `page` (records 0..n-1 of `scr`) that hold something, write their `sl` rows and text, and flag the groups that are theirs.")
  (let [^I32 ng (cg-count cg)
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 c 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 oc 0
        ^:mut ^I32 g 0
        ^:mut ^I32 keep 0
        ^:mut ^I32 row 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ts 0
        ^:mut ^I32 first 0
        ^:mut ^I32 nref 0
        ^:mut ^I32 conf 0
        ^:mut ^I32 kind 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 o 0
        ^:mut ^I32 c0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 gfl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 live 0]
    (comment "1. which candidates hold something")
    (while (< k n)
      (do (set c (* k (sm-cw)))
          (set kind (cells-at scr c))
          (set tl 0)
          (set oc 0)
          (if (!= kind (pls-signature))
            (set tl (sm-count-members scr c fw gl page)))
          (cells-set scr (+ c 11) tl)
          (set g 0)
          (while (< g ng)
            (do (if (== (cg-get cg g (cgf-page)) page)
                  (if (== (sm-group-inside cg refs owords g scr c) 1) (set oc (+ oc 1))))
                (set g (+ g 1))))
          (set keep 1)
          (if (== kind (pls-seal))
            (if (and (== (+ tl oc) 0) (!= (bit-and (cells-at scr (+ c 10)) 3) 3)) (set keep 0)))
          (if (== kind (pls-stamp))
            (if (== (+ tl oc) 0) (set keep 0)))
          (comment "a ring that is another's inner ring is part of that seal")
          (if (!= (bit-and (cells-at scr (+ c 10)) 4) 0) (set keep 0))
          (if (== keep 0) (cells-set scr c 0))
          (set k (+ k 1))))
    (comment "2. their rows")
    (set k 0)
    (while (< k n)
      (do (set c (* k (sm-cw)))
          (set kind (cells-at scr c))
          (if (> kind 0)
            (do (set tl (cells-at scr (+ c 11)))
                (set ts (cells-len et))
                (set first -1)
                (set nref 0)
                (if (and (!= kind (pls-signature)) (> tl 0))
                  (sm-text-layer-text scr c fw gl et page))
                (set g 0)
                (while (< g ng)
                  (do (if (== (cg-get cg g (cgf-page)) page)
                        (if (== (sm-group-inside cg refs owords g scr c) 1)
                          (do (if (< first 0) (set first (quot (cells-len refs) 2)))
                              (set j 0)
                              (while (< j (cg-get cg g (cgf-ocount)))
                                (do (set row (cells-at refs (+ (* (+ (cg-get cg g (cgf-ofirst)) j) 2) 1)))
                                    (rf-add refs (ea-owords) row)
                                    (set nref (+ nref 1))
                                    (if (and (== tl 0) (!= kind (pls-signature)))
                                      (do (if (> (cells-len et) ts) (cells-push et 32))
                                          (sm-push-run et (ow-get owords row (hd-tstart)) (ow-get owords row (hd-tlen)))))
                                    (set j (+ j 1)))))))
                      (set g (+ g 1))))
                (set conf 500)
                (if (== kind (pls-seal)) (set conf 600))
                (if (== kind (pls-stamp)) (set conf 700))
                (if (!= (bit-and (cells-at scr (+ c 10)) 1) 0) (set conf (+ conf 100)))
                (if (!= (bit-and (cells-at scr (+ c 10)) 2) 0) (set conf (+ conf 100)))
                (if (> tl 0) (set conf (+ conf 100)))
                (if (> conf 900) (set conf 900))
                (set o (sl-new sm page (cells-at scr (+ c 2)) (cells-at scr (+ c 3)) (cells-at scr (+ c 4)) (cells-at scr (+ c 5)) kind))
                (cells-set sm (+ (* o 16) 7) (ea-paths))
                (cells-set sm (+ (* o 16) 8) (cells-at scr (+ c 1)))
                (cells-set sm (+ (* o 16) 9) conf)
                (if (> nref 0)
                  (do (cells-set sm (+ (* o 16) 10) first)
                      (cells-set sm (+ (* o 16) 11) nref)))
                (cells-set sm (+ (* o 16) 12) (cells-at scr (+ c 10)))
                (if (> tl 0) (cells-set sm (+ (* o 16) 12) (bit-or (cells-at scr (+ c 10)) 32)))
                (cells-set sm (+ (* o 16) 13) ts)
                (cells-set sm (+ (* o 16) 14) (- (cells-len et) ts))
                (cells-set sm (+ (* o 16) 15) (cells-at scr (+ c 9)))))
          (set k (+ k 1))))
    (comment "3. the groups that are theirs: every text-layer word of the group belongs to one candidate, or the group is OCR-only and inside one")
    (set g 0)
    (while (< g ng)
      (do (if (== (cg-get cg g (cgf-page)) page)
            (do (set live 0)
                (if (> (cg-get cg g (cgf-tcount)) 0)
                  (do (set c0 -2)
                      (set j 0)
                      (while (and (< j (cg-get cg g (cgf-tcount))) (!= c0 -1))
                        (do (set row (cells-at refs (+ (* (+ (cg-get cg g (cgf-tfirst)) j) 2) 1)))
                            (set c (sm-word-cand scr n fw gl row))
                            (if (< c 0)
                              (set c0 -1)
                              (do (if (== c0 -2) (set c0 c))
                                  (if (!= c0 c) (set c0 -1))))
                            (set j (+ j 1))))
                      (if (>= c0 0) (set live 1)))
                  (do (set k 0)
                      (while (< k n)
                        (do (if (== (sm-group-inside cg refs owords g scr (* k (sm-cw))) 1) (set live 1))
                            (set k (+ k 1))))))
                (if (== live 1)
                  (do (set gfl (cg-get cg g (cgf-flags)))
                      (cg-set cg g (cgf-flags) (bit-or gfl (plg-in-seal)))))))
          (set g (+ g 1))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-find [^Cells pa ^Cells pts ^Cells gl ^Cells fw ^:mut ^Cells et ^Cells epages
                          ^:mut ^Cells cg ^:mut ^Cells refs ^Cells owords ^I32 np
                          ^:mut ^Cells sm ^:mut ^Cells scr ^:mut ^Cells tmp]
  (comment "The candidates of every page (see the head of this file) into `sm` (the `sl` arena), the text of their words appended to `et` (`sl` cells 13-14), and")
  (comment "the flag `plg-in-seal` on the groups of `cg` that are theirs. `scr` and `tmp` are scratch. Answers the candidates written.")
  (let [^I32 npaths (pa-count pa)
        ^:mut ^I32 p 1
        ^:mut ^I32 pi 0
        ^:mut ^I32 p0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 p1 0
        ^:mut ^I32 n 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ep 0
        ^:mut ^I32 pw 61200
        ^:mut ^I32 ph 79200]
    (cells-drop sm 0)
    (while (<= p np)
      (do (while (and (< pi npaths) (< (pa-get pa pi (pf-page)) p))
            (set pi (+ pi 1)))
          (set p0 pi)
          (while (and (< pi npaths) (== (pa-get pa pi (pf-page)) p))
            (set pi (+ pi 1)))
          (set p1 pi)
          (if (> p1 p0)
            (do (set ep (ev-page-row epages p))
                (if (>= ep 0)
                  (do (set pw (ep-get epages ep (epf-width)))
                      (set ph (ep-get epages ep (epf-height)))))
                (cells-drop scr 0)
                (cells-drop tmp 0)
                (cells-push tmp 0)
                (cells-push tmp 0)
                (cells-push tmp 0)
                (cells-push tmp 0)
                (cells-push tmp 0)
                (cells-push tmp 0)
                (cells-push tmp 0)
                (cells-push tmp 0)
                (set n (sm-rings pa pts p0 p1 scr tmp))
                (set n (sm-stamps pa pts p0 p1 pw ph scr n))
                (set n (sm-signatures pa pts fw et p p0 p1 pw ph scr n tmp))
                (if (> n 0) (sm-page scr n p fw gl et cg refs owords sm))))
          (set p (+ p 1))))
    (return (sl-count sm))))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- the nodes

(defn ^I32 sm-anchor [^I32 kind]
  (comment "1 for the kinds of top-level block a seal is placed by: the nodes of the flow that start somewhere on a page.")
  (if (== kind (nk-heading)) (return 1))
  (if (== kind (nk-paragraph)) (return 1))
  (if (== kind (nk-list)) (return 1))
  (if (== kind (nk-table)) (return 1))
  (if (== kind (nk-figure)) (return 1))
  (if (== kind (nk-quote)) (return 1))
  (if (== kind (nk-code)) (return 1))
  (if (== kind (nk-note)) (return 1))
  (if (== kind (nk-formula)) (return 1))
  (if (== kind (nk-caption)) (return 1))
  (return 0))

(defn ^I32 sm-min [^I32 a ^I32 b]
  (if (< a b) (return a))
  (return b))

(defn ^I32 sm-max [^I32 a ^I32 b]
  (if (> a b) (return a))
  (return b))

(defn ^I32 sm-hit [^Cells sm ^I32 o ^Cells orr ^I32 r0]
  (comment "The area (square points) of candidate `o`'s box that the regions of the chain starting at `r0` cover, on its page.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 r r0
        ^:mut ^I32 w 0
        ^:mut ^I32 h 0
        ^:mut ^I32 area 0]
    (while (>= r 0)
      (do (if (== (region-page orr r) (sl-get sm o 0))
            (do (set w (quot (- (sm-min (region-x1 orr r) (sl-get sm o 3)) (sm-max (region-x0 orr r) (sl-get sm o 1))) 100))
                (set h (quot (- (sm-min (region-y1 orr r) (sl-get sm o 4)) (sm-max (region-y0 orr r) (sl-get sm o 2))) 100))
                (if (and (> w 0) (> h 0)) (set area (+ area (* w h))))))
          (set r (region-next orr r))))
    (return area)))

(defn ^I32 sm-is-top [^Cells on ^I32 i]
  (comment "1 when node i is a block of the flow that is a child of the document or of a section.")
  (let [^I32 p (node-parent on i)]
    (if (< p 0) (return 0))
    (if (and (!= (node-kind on p) (nk-document)) (!= (node-kind on p) (nk-section))) (return 0))
    (return (sm-anchor (node-kind on i)))))

(defn ^I32 sm-below [^Cells on ^I32 i ^I32 a]
  (comment "1 when node i is a descendant of node a.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 q (node-parent on i)]
    (while (>= q 0)
      (do (if (== q a) (return 1))
          (set q (node-parent on q))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 sm-earlier [^Cells sm ^I32 a ^I32 b]
  (comment "1 when candidate a comes before candidate b in reading order: its page, then its top.")
  (if (< (sl-get sm a 0) (sl-get sm b 0)) (return 1))
  (if (and (== (sl-get sm a 0) (sl-get sm b 0)) (< (sl-get sm a 2) (sl-get sm b 2))) (return 1))
  (return 0))

(defn ^I32 sm-pending [^Cells sm ^Cells nm ^I32 n0 ^Cells on ^I32 i ^I32 page ^I32 y0 ^I32 mode]
  (comment "The next candidate to write before node i, -1 for none. `nm[n0 + o]` is the node a candidate is placed after (-1: none overlaps it). Mode 0: the")
  (comment "candidates placed after a node whose subtree has ended (i is later and not in it). Mode 1: those with no such node, whose top lies before (page, y0). Mode 2:")
  (comment "every one left. The earliest in reading order of those that qualify.")
  (let [^I32 n (sl-count sm)
        ^:mut ^I32 o 0
        ^:mut ^I32 best -1
        ^:mut ^I32 a 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ok 0]
    (while (< o n)
      (do (if (== (bit-and (sl-get sm o 12) 64) 0)
            (do (set a (cells-at nm (+ n0 o)))
                (set ok 0)
                (if (== mode 2) (set ok 1))
                (if (and (== mode 0) (>= a 0))
                  (if (and (> i a) (== (sm-below on i a) 0)) (set ok 1)))
                (if (and (== mode 1) (< a 0))
                  (if (or (< (sl-get sm o 0) page) (and (== (sl-get sm o 0) page) (< (sl-get sm o 2) y0))) (set ok 1)))
                (if (== ok 1)
                  (if (< best 0)
                    (set best o)
                    (if (== (sm-earlier sm o best) 1) (set best o))))))
          (set o (+ o 1))))
    (return best)))

(defn ^I32 sm-emit [^:mut ^Cells sm ^I32 o ^Cells et ^:mut ^Cells nodes ^:mut ^Cells attrs ^:mut ^Cells regions ^:mut ^Cells text ^I32 parent]
  (comment "Write candidate `o` as a `seal` node, the last child of `parent`: its subkind, confidence, source, region, the words as `text` (flagged `low-conf`),")
  (comment "and its colour name.")
  (let [^I32 nn (node-new nodes (nk-seal) parent)
        ^I32 tl (sl-get sm o 14)
        ^I32 ts (sl-get sm o 13)
        ^I32 fl (sl-get sm o 12)
        ^I32 hue (sm-hue (sl-get sm o 15))
        ^:mut ^I32 start 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0]
    (cells-set sm (+ (* o 16) 12) (bit-or fl 64))
    (if (< nn 0) (return -1))
    (node-set-sub nodes nn (sl-get sm o 5))
    (node-set-conf nodes nn (sl-get sm o 9))
    (node-add-src nodes nn (sr-infer))
    (node-add-region nodes regions nn (sl-get sm o 0) (sl-get sm o 1) (sl-get sm o 2) (sl-get sm o 3) (sl-get sm o 4))
    (if (> tl 0)
      (do (set start (cells-len text))
          (while (< j tl)
            (do (text-append-cp text (cells-at et (+ ts j)))
                (set j (+ j 1))))
          (node-set-text nodes nn start tl)
          (node-add-flag nodes nn (fl-low-conf))
          (if (!= (bit-and fl 32) 0) (node-add-src nodes nn (sr-text)) (node-add-src nodes nn (sr-ocr)))))
    (if (>= hue 0)
      (do (set start (cells-len text))
          (set j 0)
          (while (< j (sm-name-len hue))
            (do (text-append-cp text (sm-name-at 0 (+ (sm-name-off hue) j)))
                (set j (+ j 1))))
          (node-add-attr-text nodes attrs nn (fk-color) start (sm-name-len hue))))
    (return nn)))

(defn ^I32 sm-tail-parent [^Cells on ^Cells nm ^I32 last]
  (comment "The new node of the nearest document or section above (or at) old node `last`: what a seal left at the end is a child of (an ancestor of the last node")
  (comment "written, so the Model's preorder holds).")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 q last
        ^:mut ^I32 kq 0]
    (while (>= q 0)
      (do (set kq (node-kind on q))
          (if (or (== kq (nk-document)) (== kq (nk-section))) (return (cells-at nm q)))
          (set q (node-parent on q))))
    (return (cells-at nm 0))))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 sm-write [^:mut ^Cells sm ^Cells et ^Cells on ^Cells oa ^Cells orr ^:mut ^Cells text
                           ^:mut ^Cells nodes ^:mut ^Cells attrs ^:mut ^Cells regions ^:mut ^Cells nm]
  (comment "Copy the old Model's trees (`on oa orr`) into the empty arenas `nodes attrs regions`, in the same order, with a `seal` node for every candidate of `sm`.")
  (comment "WHERE: a candidate is drawn over the text it belongs to, and the document's own order puts it after that text (the stamp over the last lines of a paragraph,")
  (comment "the signature over the typed name). So it is written AFTER the last top-level block (a child of the document or of a section) whose region on its page")
  (comment "overlaps its box, after that block's subtree; a candidate that overlaps none is written before the first top-level block that starts below its top (the")
  (comment "later page's too). What is left is the last children of the nearest document or section above the last node written, before the first second root")
  (comment "(furniture). `nm` is scratch. Answers the seals written; the caller swaps the arenas when it is more than 0 (and leaves the old ones when it is 0).")
  (if (== (sl-count sm) 0) (return 0))
  (let [^I32 n (node-count on)
        ^I32 ns (sl-count sm)
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 p 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 o 0
        ^:mut ^I32 np 0
        ^:mut ^I32 best 0
        ^:mut ^I32 area 0
        ^:mut ^I32 pick 0
        ^:mut ^I32 placed 0]
    (cells-drop nodes 0)
    (cells-drop attrs 0)
    (cells-drop regions 0)
    (cells-drop nm 0)
    (while (< i n)
      (do (cells-push nm -1)
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (comment "the block each candidate overlaps, in nm[n + o]: the last of those that cover at least half as much of it as the one that covers most (a stamp drawn over")
    (comment "a table and the edge of the paragraph under it belongs to the table), when that is at least `sm-overlap` per cent of the candidate's box")
    (set o 0)
    (while (< o ns)
      (do (set best 0)
          (set i 0)
          (while (< i n)
            (do (if (== (sm-is-top on i) 1)
                  (do (set r (node-region-head on i))
                      (if (>= r 0)
                        (do (set area (sm-hit sm o orr r))
                            (if (> area best) (set best area))))))
                (set i (+ i 1))))
          (set pick -1)
          (if (>= (* best 100) (* (* (quot (- (sl-get sm o 3) (sl-get sm o 1)) 100) (quot (- (sl-get sm o 4) (sl-get sm o 2)) 100)) (sm-overlap)))
            (do (set i 0)
                (while (< i n)
                  (do (if (== (sm-is-top on i) 1)
                        (do (set r (node-region-head on i))
                            (if (>= r 0)
                              (if (>= (* (sm-hit sm o orr r) 2) best)
                                (if (> best 0) (set pick i))))))
                      (set i (+ i 1))))))
          (cells-push nm pick)
          (set o (+ o 1))))
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i n)
      (do (set p (node-parent on i))
          (comment "candidates whose block (and its subtree) is behind us")
          (set o (sm-pending sm nm n on i 0 0 0))
          (while (>= o 0)
            (do (set np (cells-at nm (node-parent on (cells-at nm (+ n o)))))
                (sm-emit sm o et nodes attrs regions text np)
                (set placed (+ placed 1))
                (set o (sm-pending sm nm n on i 0 0 0))))
          (comment "the first second root: whatever is left goes before it")
          (if (and (< p 0) (> i 0))
            (do (set np (sm-tail-parent on nm (- i 1)))
                (set o (sm-pending sm nm n on i 0 0 2))
                (while (>= o 0)
                  (do (sm-emit sm o et nodes attrs regions text np)
                      (set placed (+ placed 1))
                      (set o (sm-pending sm nm n on i 0 0 2))))))
          (comment "candidates that overlap no block: before the first top-level block that starts below their top")
          (if (== (sm-is-top on i) 1)
            (do (set r (node-region-head on i))
                (if (>= r 0)
                  (do (set o (sm-pending sm nm n on i (region-page orr r) (region-y0 orr r) 1))
                      (while (>= o 0)
                        (do (sm-emit sm o et nodes attrs regions text (cells-at nm p))
                            (set placed (+ placed 1))
                            (set o (sm-pending sm nm n on i (region-page orr r) (region-y0 orr r) 1))))))))
          (if (< p 0)
            (rs-node on oa orr nodes attrs regions nm i -1)
            (rs-node on oa orr nodes attrs regions nm i (cells-at nm p)))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (comment "after the last node: the candidates left")
    (set np (sm-tail-parent on nm (- n 1)))
    (set o (sm-pending sm nm n on n 0 0 2))
    (while (>= o 0)
      (do (sm-emit sm o et nodes attrs regions text np)
          (set placed (+ placed 1))
          (set o (sm-pending sm nm n on n 0 0 2))))
    (cells-drop nm n)
    (rs-remap attrs nm)
    (return placed)))
